---
title: Breakfast Biscuits
servings: 12
cuisine: american
main_protein: dairy
prep_time: "20 minutes"
cook_time: "25 minutes"
tags:
  - breakfast
image: ../obsidian/attachments/Pasted image 20260216195426.jpg
leftover_portions: 8
prep:
  - Preheat oven to 400°F
  - Line a baking tray with parchment paper
  - Blend 450 g cottage cheese
  - Shred 1.5 cups cheddar cheese
  - Cook the sausage
---
Preheat the #oven{} 400F and line a #baking tray{} with parchment paper.

In a medium mixing bowl whisk together @cottage cheese{450%g}, blended, and @eggs{4}. In a separate medium mixing bowl, combine @all purpose flour{2.5%cups}, ground flax seed, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, red pepper flakes, @baking powder{1%tbsp} and salt.

Slowly add the dry ingredients into the wet ingredients, mixing well.

Add mix-ins including vegetables, herbs and cooked meat along with 1 cup of the @cheddar cheese{1.5%cups}, shredded and divided, and the @sausage{}. Mix until the ingredients are fully combined (you may need to use your hands to ensure everything is fully incorporated.)

Lightly flour your hands and divide the dough into 12 even-sized 1-inch thick round disk shaped biscuits (about ⅓ cup of batter in each). Arrange the biscuits on the prepared baking tray (please note depending on the size of your tray you may need to use 2 trays to ensure the biscuits are evenly spaced). Sprinkle the tops with the remaining cheese.

Bake at 400F for ~{5%minutes}, decrease the temperature to 350F and bake for an additional ~{20%minutes} (do not open the oven in between). Once the bottom of the biscuits are golden brown and the tops are just beginning to brown, your biscuits are done!
